{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDjvv259DqQgWAzmTvc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it in `money.py:5-6`. Before, every person got `total // people` and the remainder was thrown away. Now the leftover grosze go one each to the first people in the list:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\nI ran a quick inline check, not a test file. It covered seven cases: 100/3, 100/1, 99/3, 0/4, 5/7, -100/3 and 101/4. In every case the shares add up to the total, the list length equals the number of people, and no two shares differ by more than 1 grosz. Refunds, which are negative totals, also add up: -100/3 gives `[-33, -33, -34]`.\n\nTwo things to know:\n- **The first people in the list always get the extra grosz.** Make sure that's acceptable for whoever is listed first, such as the bill's creator.\n- **Nothing is committed or deployed.** The change is only in the working tree, so it's yours to commit and ship. Next sprint, the cases above would make good starting tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":782,"cache_read_input_tokens":17867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":782},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94bc93d5-f14e-4d0a-8190-be803fb4dac5","uuid":"bf9cc0b5-63f8-4585-9d04-ef9f28ac44f9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:20:11.897Z","request_id":"req_011CggDjvfeH4JZSJ7nJXTyg"}
